module v2.test.fixture.concept_index_pool.concepts

data concept_index_pool_fixture_note: String = "The enumeration subjects for v2.test.claim.concept_index_enumeration's parse-only witnesses, and the POOL those witnesses scan. They live in a directory of their own because the pool root is an input whose SIZE is the witness's cost: concept_decl_facts parses every .dag under the root on every call, so a root of src/v2/test/claim made each witness parse 638 files / ~3.0 MB and grow with every unrelated module added anywhere beneath it. That is what pushed witness_coproduct_arms_parse_only past the 5000ms fast-lane budget (6065ms thread-CPU, CI run 31017039134) and rehomed it to test/claim/long/ under PR #7756. Breadth was never the subject: every assertion names one concept by qualified name and checks its extracted fields, so the requirement is a pool containing those concepts, and the smallest pool that crosses the boundary is this one (operator ruling 2026-08-04 — a witness's size is DERIVED from what it proves, never chosen for verisimilitude). These types are declared, never constructed; they exist to be READ by the concept index, which is why the fixture is a plain module and not a _test.dag."

type ConceptIndexWitnessRecord {
  alpha: String
  beta: Bool
}

type ConceptIndexWitnessRecordPerturb {
  alpha: String
  beta: Int
}

type ConceptIndexWitnessCoproduct =
  | NullaryArm
  | NamedFieldArm { alpha: String, beta: Bool }
